.TH "ANI-CLI" "1" "August 2026" "ani-cli" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ani-cli \- watch anime from the commandline
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ani-cli
[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A shell script to browse and search anime from the command-line.
.PD 0
.P
.PD
This tool scrapes the site hianime.at.
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\f[B]ani-cli\f[R] without options defaults to iina on macOS, flatpak mpv on Linux (if available), mpv apk on android, vlc on iOS and mpv media player everywhere else.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-e | --episode | -r | --range\fR \fI\,<episode>\/\fR
Specify the episode numbers to watch. If range is specified it should be quoted or separated by a non-numeric character (eg. -).
.TP
\fB\-c | --continue\fR
Continue watching anime from history.
.TP
\fB\--resume\fR
Resume playback from the last saved position (mpv only).
.TP
\fB\-d | --download\fR
Download episode.
.TP
\fB\-D | --delete\fR
Delete history.
.TP
\fB\-l | --logview\fR
Show logs.
.TP
\fB\-h | --help\fR
Show summary of options.
.TP
\fB\-q | --quality\fR \fI\,<best|worst|360|480|720|1080>\/\fR
Set the video quality. Default quality is best.
.TP
\fB\-s | --syncplay\fR
Watch anime together with friends, using Syncplay (works with mpv only).
.TP
\fB\-U | --update\fR
Fetch update from github.
.TP
\fB\-v | --vlc\fR
Use VLC as the media player.
.TP
\fB\-S | --select-nth\fR \fI\,<index>\/\fR
Selects nth entry.
.TP
\fB\-P | --page\fR \fI\,<page>\/\fR
Search page number to start from (25 results per page). The search menu also offers a "load more results" entry to page interactively.
.TP
\fB\--parallel\fR \fI\,<jobs>\/\fR
Download up to \fI\,<jobs>\/\fR episodes concurrently with --batch. Default is 1 (sequential).
.TP
\fB\--auto-play\fR
Keep playing the following episodes automatically when one finishes (mpv only).
.TP
\fB\-N | --nextep-countdown\fR
Prints a countdown to the next episode as the last episode in the list. If in history is after the current episode.
.TP
\fB\--dub\fR
Play the dubbed version. Without this flag, it'll always play the subbed version.
.TP
\fB\--rofi\fR
Use rofi instead of fzf for the interactive menu
.TP
\fB\--skip\fR
Skip the intro/outro of the episode (mpv only). Uses the bundled aniskip integration (queries api.aniskip.com via the MyAnimeList id the embed provides), falling back to the ani-skip binary if it is installed.
.TP
\fB\--no-detach\fR
Don't detach the player (useful for in-terminal playback, mpv only)
.TP
\fB\--exit-after-play\fR
Exit the player, and return the player exit code (useful for non interactive scenarios, mpv only)
.TP
\fB\--cache-size\fR
mpv buffer window kept for seeking in both directions, as a bytesize (eg. 1GiB). Default is 1GiB, or whatever \fBANI_CLI_CACHE\fR is set to. A small window evicts already-played data, so backward seeking silently stops working near the start of the episode.
.TP
\fB\--disk-cache\fR, \fB\--no-disk-cache\fR
Spill the mpv stream cache to a temporary file instead of RAM, so long episodes and movies stay seekable in both directions regardless of the ram window. Enabled by default; disable with \fB\--no-disk-cache\fR or \fBANI_CLI_DISK_CACHE=0\fR.
.TP
\fB\--batch\fR
Download all episodes of found anime (with progress).
.TP
\fB\--dmenu\fR
Use dmenu instead of fzf for the interactive menu.
.PP
.SH
ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.PP
ani-cli v5 uses environment variables to control unstable/untested and niche features in addition to everything that has an option. Command-line options take precedence over env vars. Note that these are all subject to change.
.TP
\fBANI_CLI_MODE\fR
Controls the scraped media's mode, valid options are sub or dub. Default is sub.
.TP
\fBANI_CLI_DOWNLOAD_DIR\fR
Controls the directory where files are downloaded. Downloads are placed in a per-anime subfolder (eg. $DOWNLOAD_DIR/One Piece/Episode 1.mp4). Default is the current dir.
.TP
\fBANI_CLI_PARALLEL\fR
Controls how many episodes are downloaded concurrently with --batch. Equivalent to --parallel. Default is 1.
.TP
\fBANI_CLI_CACHE\fR
mpv buffer window kept for seeking, applied symmetrically so you can seek both forward and backward. Bytesize (eg. 512MiB, 2GiB). Default is 1GiB. Note that a value of 0 disables the back buffer entirely (forward seek range starts after the current position); prefer a size instead.
.TP
\fBANI_CLI_DISK_CACHE\fR
Controls whether the mpv stream cache is spilled to a temporary file so long episodes stay seekable backward. Can be 0 (RAM only) or 1 (on disk). Default is 1, equivalent to \fB\--disk-cache\fR.
.TP
\fBANI_CLI_AUTO_PLAY\fR
Controls if episodes play one after another automatically (mpv only). Equivalent to --auto-play. Can be 0 (disabled) or 1 (enabled). Default is 0.
.TP
\fBANI_CLI_QUALITY\fR
Controls the scraped media's quality, check hianime.at for valid options or set to worst/best. Default is best.
.TP
\fBANI_CLI_PLAYER\fR
Sets the player ani-cli uses. Can be debug (print links), download (equivalent to -d), android_mpv (apk and am start), android_vlc (apk and am start), flatpak_mpv (for flatpak), catt (for streaming to tv), or any player that can play urls. For defaults see working without arguments.
.TP
\fBANI_CLI_PLAYER_FLAGS\fR
Extra flags to pass to the player. Default is empty.
.TP
\fBANI_CLI_MENU\fR
Controls the frontend of ani-cli. Can be fzf, rofi, or dmenu. Default is fzf.
.TP
\fBANI_CLI_MENU_FLAGS\fR
Extra flags to pass to the menu program. Default is empty.
.TP
\fBANI_CLI_LOG\fR
Controls the logging feature for playback. Can be 1(logs) or 0(doesn't log). Default is 1.
.TP
\fBANI_CLI_HIST_DIR\fR
Controls the directory ani-cli uses for storing history. A /ani-cli subfolder is created there for the histfile if doesn't exists. Default is $XDG_STATE_HOME if set, $HOME/.local/state if not.
.TP
\fBANI_CLI_SKIP_INTRO\fR
Controls if intros/outros are skipped (works with mpv only). Uses the bundled aniskip integration, or the ani-skip binary if installed. Can be 0 (disabled) or 1 (enabled). Default is 0.
.TP
\fBANI_CLI_NO_DETACH\fR
Controls if mpv is detached from the main process for playback, which can be useful for use with terminal renderers such as kitty. (works with mpv only). Can be 0 (disabled) or 1 (enabled). Default is 0.
.TP
\fBANI_CLI_EXIT_AFTER_PLAY\fR
Controls if ani-cli exits after playback finishes, returning the player's exit code (useful for non interactive scenarios, mpv only). Implies ANI_CLI_NO_DETACH=1. Can be 0 (disabled) or 1 (enabled). Default is 0.
.TP
\fBANI_CLI_BRANCH\fR
Controls the branch used for updates. Default is master.
.PP
.SH EPISODE SELECTION
.PP
Multiple episodes can be chosen using fzf (or alternative frontend's) multi-selection mode. For this refer to their instructions.
